target:    tests/docker/lib.sh
gate:      php tests/rehearsal-vintage-corpus-test.php
kind:      restore-defect
expect:    the vintage installer persists the version its own init_tables only set in memory
rationale: Every vintage's init_tables() closes with a comment saying it saves the version in the database and an assignment that only touches the in-memory array; the arm persists it from slimstat_save_options() on the shutdown of a real request, and `wp eval` has no shutdown. Drop these two lines and the options row carries no version key, which is not a visible state -- every later read goes through the defaults merge and returns a plausible version. The corpus builder shares this helper, so the same silence would be baked into the corpus the cell is then judged against.
---
--- a/tests/docker/lib.sh
+++ b/tests/docker/lib.sh
@@ -226,8 +226,6 @@
            4.8.x block is skipped. Persisted through the ARM own saver wherever it has one, so
            this reproduces what a real first request leaves behind rather than inventing a row.
            PITFALLS 133. */
-        if (method_exists("wp_slimstat", "slimstat_save_options")) { wp_slimstat::slimstat_save_options(); }
-        else { update_option("slimstat_options", wp_slimstat::$settings); }
         echo $f;
       }
     }'
